description:
Tools store shortcuts as text, such as `"Ctrl+Shift+S"`. Write

```cpp
struct Chord { bool ctrl{ false }, shift{ false }, alt{ false }; std::string key; };

bool parseShortcut(const std::string& text, Chord& out);
std::string formatShortcut(const Chord& c);
```

`parseShortcut`:

- parts are separated by `+`; spaces around them are ignored; names ignore case;
- the modifiers are `Ctrl` (also `Control`), `Shift` and `Alt`, each at most once;
- exactly one part is the key, and it comes **last**: a single letter or digit (stored in upper case, `"S"`), `F1` to `F12`, or one of `Enter`, `Escape`, `Space`, `Tab`, `Delete` (stored with that spelling);
- anything else returns `false`.

`formatShortcut` writes the modifiers in the order Ctrl, Shift, Alt, then the key, joined with `+`: `"Ctrl+Shift+S"`.

